scene W: {N} said no to {mentor} once, out of duty to others, and has wondered ever since. This smaller ask fits around those duties.
scene U: {N} looks at {mentor}'s offer closely. A few weekends would show {N}, at last, what the old road was really like.
scene B: The old chance with {mentor} is gone for good. A small part of it now could still open other doors, if played well.
scene R: {Ns} heart jumps. {mentor} remembered. All these years {N} has thought about that no, and here is a little yes on offer.
scene G: Not every tree bears in its first season. {mentor} is offering a cutting from the old one, small but alive.
scene gone: {mentor} is not here to offer it. But a call for weekend helpers in {mentor}'s old field brings back the no that {N} has never quite stopped turning over.
