- R | say yes before they have finished the sentence | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 86
- G | say no gently; that road was never the right one, and that is all right | identity | v: tradition (accepting what is) | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 74
- W>U | agree, and ask to learn one skill properly while there | v: self-direction, conformity | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
- U>B | use the weekends to meet the people who now run that world | v: power, achievement | chance: 62
- B>R | hold out for the most exciting part of the work, and only that | v: stimulation, power | chance: 62
- R>G | bring a young relative along, to see that world early | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 75
- G>W | offer to help with the quiet background work that nobody sees | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 82
works: The weekends with {mentor} fill a gap {N} had stopped noticing.
works: The old regret eases, and {N} sees that road as it really was.
fails: The small part only shows how much of the big one {N} missed.
fails: Time runs too tight, and {mentor} is let down a second time.

